Figure 4 demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are actively transported to the draining lymph node by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). The percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells in the lymph node peaks at day 2 post-immunization. Migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) account for the majority (60-80%) of Nano-11-positive cells, and these cells also exhibit a significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity of Nano-11 per cell, indicating more efficient uptake compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs and monocytes/macrophages.